# PHP Backend (Fantager)

Quick ref: `docs/guides/backend.md`. API spec: `docs/architecture/api.md`. Entities: `docs/architecture/entities.md`.

## Before implementing

- Check `docs/product/known-issues.md` (Open rows and Later product decisions), matching `docs/systems/*.md` Remaining work, and matching `docs/screens/*.md`
- Read matching `docs/systems/*.md` and `docs/screens/*.md`
- Find an existing feature in the same domain and follow its patterns

## Hero level (locked — #6)

- `Hero.xp` is a lifetime total; never subtract it on level-up.
- `Hero.level` is the live truth. Do not derive level from XP on read (Twig, API, combat snapshots).
- After awarding match XP, update stored level with the **current** curve. When the curve or `Kingdom.level_cap` changes, rewrite levels with a migration or job — never lazy-recalc on request.
- Spec: `docs/systems/hero-system.md` § Locked: hero level invariant. Curve: `config/game/hero-progression.yaml`. Do not invent a new curve on read.

## Team chemistry (locked — #7)

- `Team.chemistry` is flavor for matches. Combat and in-match morale must not read it.
- Live consumers: dashboard / history, `FanClubService` target and show-up, league standings tie-break.
- Do not add combat pairing tables or skip Loners in the chemistry formula. In-combat synergy is Cut (#9).
- Spec: `docs/systems/team-system.md` § Locked: chemistry flavor.

## Item occupancy (locked — #8)

- Nine slots including `ring_2`. Ring items equip in `ring` or `ring_2`.
- Two-handed subtypes (`two_handed_*`, bow, crossbow, staff) occupy both hands.
- Dual-wield: one-handed sword/axe/mace and dagger in `off_hand`. Do not add extra swings or targeting lists.
- Giant/Ent restrictions stay `RaceConfig`. Spec: `docs/systems/item-system.md` § Locked: item occupancy.

## Haste / Shock initiative (locked — #9 slice)

- YAML `speed_bonus_percent` / `speed_reduction_percent` apply to the per-round turn **sort** after status ticks.
- Do not apply them to AP or stored `derived.baseInitiative`. Additive; clamp modifier at 0.
- Spec: `docs/systems/combat-formulas.md` § Speed / Initiative.

## In-combat morale (Cut — #9 slice)

- Do not emit `morale_change`. Combat must not read `moraleDecayMultiplier`.
- Volatile / Battle Hardened player copy is flavor. Kickoff damage band and post-match morale stay.

## Race synergy / simulate (Cut — #9)

- Do not add in-combat race/role synergy tables. Combat must not read `ignoresRaceSynergy`.
- Do not ship `POST /api/v1/combat/simulate`. The route is **Cut** (no controller). Friendly matches are the live adjacent path.
- Spec: `docs/systems/combat-system.md` § Locked: no race synergy / no simulate.

## Public wiki (Planned — A8.5)

- Do not ship `GET /wiki`, a wiki entity, or a Help navbar link. Route stays Planned.
- Live public content is homepage + `/news` (seed / DB; no admin CMS).
- Spec: `docs/screens/00-public-pages.md` § Locked: public wiki stays Planned.

## Password change / extra settings (Planned — A8.6)

- Do not ship session password change, notification prefs, privacy flags, or `GET/PUT /api/v1/settings`.
- Live settings stay language, backdrop-close, email change, and account deletion. Forgotten passwords use `/password-reset`.
- Spec: `docs/screens/19-player-profile-settings.md` § Locked: password change / extra settings stay Planned.

## Formation L1/L2 (locked — #12)

- Per-slot `target_order` + `fallback` and thin equipped `spell_priorities` are live.
- Do not add L3 action sequences or expose `enemy_status` / `lowest_hp_enemy` in the player UI.
- Save goes through `FormationTacticsNormalizer`. Spec: `docs/systems/formation-system.md` § Locked: L1/L2 editor.

## Roster extras (Cut — #13)

- Do not add batch training, multi-select, or server-side roster filter/sort query params.
- Train / equip / spells / sell stay on hero detail and `/app/training`, not the roster grid.
- Spec: `docs/screens/03-hero-roster.md` § Locked: roster extras.

## Genie summon pool (locked — #14)

- Compatible races use relationship ≥ 50, except Genie adaptation ≥ 80 (Genie / Human / Elf).
- Same pool for player summons, NPC daily summons, NPC marketplace hero buys, and kingdom starting roster.
- Do not restore a Genie-only NPC buy filter or a Genie-only starting roster.
- Spec: `docs/systems/summoning-system.md` § Locked: Genie summon pool.

## Marketplace price band (locked — #15)

- Listing buy-now / start / buyout must sit in `[round(suggested × 0.5), round(suggested × 2)]` (min 1 gold).
- Suggested: heroes/trainers `HeroRatingCalculator::estimateMarketPrice()`; items `ItemService::estimateMarketPrice()`.
- Auction bids are not capped. Do not add a second pricing formula.
- Spec: `docs/systems/marketplace-system.md` § Locked: listing price band.

## Spell catalog (locked — #16)

- Seeded library is two spells per school per tier for T1–T5 (`required_mastery_tier` = `tier`).
- Do not add T6+, resurrection, summon-creature, or new combat effect keys.
- Combat uses school + type + `spell.tier`. Spec: `docs/systems/spell-system.md` § Locked: catalog T1–T5.

## Arena analytics (locked — #4)

- HQ panel graphs/history from the last 18 `arena_revenue` payouts. Same window for table, chart, and summary.
- Do not add a new analytics route, season query, snapshot entity, home-advantage, or match results on the table.
- Spec: `docs/screens/18-arena-management.md` § Locked: attendance analytics.

## Item enchanting (locked — #2)

- Enchanting is not in the live game. Do not reintroduce essence or ship an enchant UI, cost, or combat effect.
- `Item.special_effects` stays unused. Combat reads `bonuses` only. Do not drop the column in this alignment.
- Spec: `docs/systems/item-system.md` § Locked: no enchanting. A later product decision is required before adding enchanting.

## Layering

- **Controllers** (`Controller/Web`, `Controller/Api/V1`): routing, auth, input parsing, response only
- **Services** (`Service/{Domain}/`): all business logic — shared by Web and API
- **Repositories**: queries only
- Never duplicate logic between Web and API controllers

## API (`Controller/Api/V1`)

- `use ApiControllerTrait;`
- Errors: `jsonError('translation.key', $status)` — never hardcoded English
- Caught exceptions: `jsonException($e, 422)`
- Register new routes in `docs/architecture/routes.md`

## Web (`Controller/Web`)

- `UserMessageTranslator` for flashes; Twig for rendering
- Authenticated routes: `#[IsGranted('ROLE_PLAYER')]`, paths under `/app/`

## Services & exceptions

- `declare(strict_types=1);` on every file
- Business rule violations: `throw new UserFacingException('error.key', $params)`
- Translation keys in `translations/messages.en.yaml` and `translations/messages.cs.yaml`

## Tests

- `tests/Service/{Domain}/` for unit tests; mirror `src/Service/` structure
- Add tests for new logic; do not run PHPUnit unless the user asks (see `AGENTS.md`)

## Schema & docs

- New entity/enum → update `docs/architecture/entities.md`
- New route → update `docs/architecture/routes.md`
- Feature status change → update `docs/systems/README.md` status snapshot and the reader snapshot in `docs/product/progress.md` (plus the compact table in `README.md` § Game progress)

## Optional verification (user-requested only)

```bash
docker exec -u apache fantager-web composer test
docker exec -u apache fantager-web composer phpstan
docker exec -u apache fantager-web composer php-cs
bash scripts/check-backend-docs.sh
```

## No automatic commands

Do not run `composer test`, PHPStan, php-cs, `check-backend-docs.sh`, migrations, `composer init-db`, or Docker verify commands unless the user explicitly requests them.
